lantation in Children with Single-Sided Deafness: : Preoperative Assessment and Device Use","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-787984","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Due to constant antigenic drift and shift, current influenza-A vaccines need to be redesigned and administered annually. A universal flu vaccine (UFV) that provides long-lasting protection against both seasonal and emerging pandemic influenza strains is thus urgently needed. The hemagglutinin (HA) stem antigen is a promising target for such a vaccine as it contains neutralizing epitopes, known to induce cross-protective IgG responses against a wide variety of influenza subtypes. In this study, we describe the development of a UFV candidate consisting of a HAstem trimer displayed on the surface of rigid capsid-like particles (CLP). Compared to soluble unconjugated HAstem trimer, the CLP-HAstem particles induced a more potent, long-lasting immune response and were able to protect mice against both homologous and heterologous H1N1 influenza challenge, even after a single dose.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Thrane, Susan","Aves, Kara Lee","Uddbäck, Ida","Janitzek, Christoph M","Han, Julianna","Yang, Yuhe R","Ward, Andrew B","Theander, Thor G","Nielsen, Morten A","Salanti, Ali","Thomsen, Allan Randrup","Christensen, Jan Pravsgaard","Sander, Adam F."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-439364"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Scripps Research Institute"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a vaccine displaying a trimeric influenza a ha stem protein on capsid like particles elicits potent and long lasting protection in mice","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/vaccines8030389","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-439364","identifier":[{"id":"32679905","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85088486447","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7564254","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-4d031886-1db9-4f5c-8feb-65aceb08d056"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2A3BE3592FDF83AF075CE6A1DE871D7F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/vaccines8030389","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/247548114/vaccines_08_00389_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, CMP","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, VAR2CSA team"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"scripps research institute","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Scripps Research Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Susan","key":"thranepau","last":"Thrane","locid":"53d6327a-d6bb-422f-909b-58ce29750b98","name":"Thrane, Susan","orcid":"0000-0001-6596-3527","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kara-Lee","key":"avespau","last":"Aves","locid":"60399d84-f32e-4ada-8a1e-f4154261954f","name":"Aves, Kara Lee","name_org":"Aves, Kara-Lee","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ida E M","key":"uddbäckpau","last":"Uddbäck","locid":"90b20ba7-7940-44a0-94a9-915006cc1343","name":"Uddbäck, Ida","name_org":"Uddbäck, Ida E M","orcid":"0000-0001-6007-5918","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christoph M","key":"janitzekpau","last":"Janitzek","locid":"77b70919-622d-4eb8-9793-47cbf3a0ec74","name":"Janitzek, Christoph M","orcid":"0000-0001-6529-9355","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Julianna","key":"hanpau","last":"Han","name":"Han, Julianna","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Yuhe R","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Yuhe R","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Andrew B","key":"wardpau","last":"Ward","name":"Ward, Andrew B","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thor G","key":"theanderpau","last":"Theander","locid":"e84d9c51-0ab1-425a-8369-42fff90fdce0","name":"Theander, Thor G","orcid":"0000-0002-3509-7514","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten A","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"fb98e249-1036-4c83-b6f6-9b6dae9a2b19","name":"Nielsen, Morten A","orcid":"0000-0003-2668-4992","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ali","key":"salantipau","last":"Salanti","locid":"59059650-0fee-44f7-a4c2-8b6281d02db5","name":"Salanti, Ali","orcid":"0000-0003-2207-5575","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Allan R","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"fdf0ac42-94d9-4cd6-ae66-be91f73c0dbe","name":"Thomsen, Allan Randrup","name_org":"Thomsen, Allan R","orcid":"0000-0002-2392-9803","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jan P","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"042fb583-4cb8-4de1-bcb5-5ac3b53d0d48","name":"Christensen, Jan Pravsgaard","name_org":"Christensen, Jan P","orcid":"0000-0002-4299-9479","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Adam F","key":"sanderpau","last":"Sander","locid":"07a898e8-c200-4445-95ef-37df710168ff","name":"Sander, Adam F.","name_org":"Sander, Adam F","orcid":"0000-0002-8782-7830","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32679905"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/vaccines8030389","issn":["2076393X"],"issue":"3","journal":"Vaccines","paperid":"389","status":"p","title":"Vaccines","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85088486447"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4d031886-1db9-4f5c-8feb-65aceb08d056"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A vaccine displaying a trimeric influenza-A HA stem protein on capsid-like particles elicits potent and long-lasting protection in mice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-439364","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Alzheimer's disease (AD) is the most common cause of dementia and early and accurate diagnosis is important. Olfactory dysfunction is an early sign of AD. The contribution by test of olfactory function has been surveyed in AD vs a line of conditions but remains to be settled in the workup of unselected patients referred with suspected dementia. METHODS: We performed a two-step investigation: first, a comparative study of healthy controls and probable AD patients to test the applicability of the chosen scents (cuisine study); second, a study of consecutive patients referred to our geriatric outpatient clinic for suspected dementia with the investigating personnel blinded to the results of the Olfactory Test (blinded study). RESULTS: The sum of scents detected discriminated patients with probable AD from controls in the cuisine study (n = 40; p < 0.001; area under ROC curve 0.94). In the blinded study (n = 50) the diagnosis was probable AD in 48%, minimal cognitive impairment in 24%, vascular dementia in 8%, alcohol induced impairment in 12%, depression in 4%, and Parkinson's disease and Lewy body dementia in 2%. Area under the ROC-curve was 0.67. The odds ratio for probable AD with 2+ smell errors was 12 (95%-CI: 1.3-101; p = 0.026 (reference 0-1 smell errors)) age adjusted. None in the AD group had zero smell errors (Negative Predictive Value 100%). CONCLUSION: Olfactory testing may support to dismiss the diagnosis of probable AD in the workup of a mixed group of patients referred with cognitive impairment. Still, it had a low sensitivity for probable AD.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Christensen, Ib Thrane","Larsson, Elna-Marie","Holm, Ida Elisabeth","Faurholt Nielsen, Ole Bruno","Andersen, Stig"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-073809"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"olfactory testing in consecutive patients referred with suspected dementia","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12877-017-0516-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-073809","identifier":[{"id":"85020944020","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28633628","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000405857400001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-51d3749e-df1c-450a-ace1-2cef4190aa06"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F9365F0D32CC12A6EA32B8CF9745155A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/268586743/Open_Access_Article.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12877-017-0516-2","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Geriatri [Klinik Akut]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Akut"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ib Thrane","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"87e1edd4-f584-4942-9517-943bb8a91cb1","name":"Christensen, Ib Thrane","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":nul